      "title": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7a9dfc23-1ae0-53bf-8955-abf0621aa9e5",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y &=8 \\\\ 4x-7y &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=4 \\\\ y &=-2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-2)=4\\,\u21d2\\,x=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3a184c5a-5027-50f8-8022-6be18f4bee9e",
